{
	"_note": [
		"Seed vocabulary for monster_gen.py --custom. These are PROMPTING MATERIAL, not",
		"output: the script hands a few of them over so a model has something specific to",
		"synthesise a name, instinct, moves and description from, instead of inventing from",
		"a blank page. Nothing here is meant to be read aloud verbatim.",
		"",
		"Themes union when several are given (--theme cavern,undead). To add a theme -",
		"including tone tags with no rulebook setting, like 'comical' or 'airborne' - add a",
		"key under 'themes' with every category below filled in. tools/validate_skill.py",
		"enforces that every theme carries every category and that none are empty.",
		"",
		"Categories, and what each feeds:",
		"  substance  terrain/material, first half of a compound name (Mud-, Gravel-)",
		"  bodypart   second half of a compound name (-scale, -fang, -maw)",
		"  action     agentive forms (Bone-Eater) and move priming",
		"  texture    adjectives for the description line",
		"  drive      instinct priming - phrased to follow 'Instinct: '",
		"  sound      onomatopoeia fragments for noises and Skree-Fang style names",
		"  quality    terse fictional capability, bestiary style (Burrowing, Camouflage)",
		"  evocative  whole surprising details - the catch-all for anything without its",
		"             own table. These are the highest-surprisal entries and the most",
		"             likely to produce a creature a model would not have converged on.",
		"",
		"",
		"WHEN ADDING OR EDITING A THEME THAT MIRRORS A BESTIARY SETTING, READ THE",
		"ROSTER FIRST. Every theme here was originally written from the setting's",
		"NAME and every one of them came out skewed. 'Lower Depths' sounds oceanic,",
		"so it was written as pressure and brine - but its roster is two dragons,",
		"two fire creatures and three deep elves, with barely anything aquatic.",
		"'Ravenous Hordes' was written as an insect hive; 15 of its 19 monsters are",
		"orc, gnoll and triton warbands. 'Dark Woods' was written as trees; only 2",
		"of 18 are plants. To check, list the setting's monsters and write toward",
		"what is actually in it:",
		"  monster_gen.py --setting-info <tag>",
		"",
		"Tone tags with no rulebook setting ('comical', 'airborne') have no roster",
		"to check against, so that discipline does not apply - but they are also the",
		"ones most likely to drift toward a single narrow reading, so pick a handful",
		"of imagined creatures first and write toward the spread, not the label.",
		"",
		"Naming patterns these feed are documented in",
		"references/treasure-and-monster-building.md."
	],
